| 165 | an operator is not a function value: `applyIt(opr ×, a, b)` is refused at parse time, and `(×)` or a bare `×` in argument position raises an `InterpreterBug` under walk | NEGATIVE-VERIFIED | design limit (specification) | `Specification/appendices/grammars/concrete-syntax.tex`, "Expressions" | none | run-c3 | siblings: 156. No production of the grammar makes an operator a primary expression. `opr ×` as an argument: `Operator declarations are not allowed in block expressions.` (`parser/preparser/PreParserState.java:173`). `(×)` or `×`: `** bug! The number of parameters (2) does not match with the number of arguments (0).` (`values/NonPrimitive.java:216`): walk applies the declaration to no arguments, an implementation gap (walk). A plain function and a lambda are values. Workaround: eta-expand, `fn (p, q) => p × q`. Probes `explorations/run-c3/probes/lift_g3.fss` and, beside it, `lift_g3b`, `lift_g3d` (fail) and `lift_g3c` (works), in the parent of a0a0c7c99. full text: history, row 165 |
